-- ccc26-probation-orders.l4 -- sections 732.11, 732.2, 733 and 733.1 of the Criminal Code (Canada), R.S.C., 1985, c. C-46: the use of samples and their results,
-- the coming into force, duration and change of a probation order, its transfer, and the offence of failing to comply (lines 15594-15643 of the text).
-- Layer 1 of part ccc26. The text is a plain-text rendering, made by a converter script, of the Justice Laws Website consolidation; it is not the official
-- text and nothing here is claimed verified against the official text.

§ `Section 732.11 -- Prohibition on use of bodily substance`

-- (1): a flat negative with an "except": the use for the stated purpose is not barred by this subsection.
-- src:15594 | Prohibition on use of bodily substance
-- src:15595 | 732.11 (1) No person shall use a bodily substance provided under a probation order except for the purpose of determining whether an offender is complying with a condition of the order that they abstain from the consumption of drugs, alcohol or any other intoxicating substance.
@ref s 732.11(1) (src:15594-15595)
GIVEN `the bodily substance was provided under a probation order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the use is for the purpose of determining whether an offender is complying with a condition of the order that they abstain from the consumption of drugs, alcohol or any other intoxicating substance` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 732.11(1) the use of the bodily substance is barred` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the bodily substance was provided under a probation order` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "No person shall use a bodily substance provided under a probation order"
        IF `the use is for the purpose of determining whether an offender is complying with a condition of the order that they abstain from the consumption of drugs, alcohol or any other intoxicating substance` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "except for the purpose of determining whether an offender is complying with a condition of the order that they abstain from the consumption of drugs, alcohol or any other intoxicating substance"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- (3): the exception to (2). It permits three uses of the results; it does not say that any other use is barred (that is (2)'s work).
-- src:15598 | Exception
-- src:15599 | (3) The results of the analysis of a bodily substance provided under a probation order may be disclosed to the offender to whom they relate, and may also be used or disclosed in the course of an investigation of, or in a proceeding for, an offence under section 733.1 or, if the results are made anonymous, for statistical or other research purposes.
@ref s 732.11(3) (src:15598-15599)
GIVEN `the results are disclosed to the offender to whom they relate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the results are used or disclosed in the course of an investigation of, or in a proceeding for, an offence under section 733.1` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the results are made anonymous` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the results are used or disclosed for statistical or other research purposes` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 732.11(3) the results may be used or disclosed` MEANS   -- gate: if (the results are made anonymous), for research use
    BRANCH
        IF `the results are disclosed to the offender to whom they relate` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the results are used or disclosed in the course of an investigation of, or in a proceeding for, an offence under section 733.1` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the results are made anonymous` AND `the results are used or disclosed for statistical or other research purposes` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may be disclosed to the offender to whom they relate, and may also be used or disclosed in the course of an investigation of, or in a proceeding for, an offence under section 733.1 or, if the results are made anonymous, for statistical or other research purposes"

-- (2): "Subject to subsection (3), no person shall use, disclose or allow the disclosure of the results of the analysis of a bodily substance provided under a probation order".
-- src:15596 | Prohibition on use or disclosure of result
-- src:15597 | (2) Subject to subsection (3), no person shall use, disclose or allow the disclosure of the results of the analysis of a bodily substance provided under a probation order.
@ref s 732.11(2) (src:15596-15597)
GIVEN `the results are of the analysis of a bodily substance provided under a probation order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the results are disclosed to the offender to whom they relate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the results are used or disclosed in the course of an investigation of, or in a proceeding for, an offence under section 733.1` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the results are made anonymous` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the results are used or disclosed for statistical or other research purposes` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 732.11(2) the use or disclosure of the results is barred` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the results are of the analysis of a bodily substance provided under a probation order` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the results of the analysis of a bodily substance provided under a probation order"
        IF `s 732.11(3) the results may be used or disclosed` `the results are disclosed to the offender to whom they relate` `the results are used or disclosed in the course of an investigation of, or in a proceeding for, an offence under section 733.1` `the results are made anonymous` `the results are used or disclosed for statistical or other research purposes` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subject to subsection (3), no person shall use, disclose or allow the disclosure of the results"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- (4): the offence, and its punishment (summary conviction only; the penalty itself is in section 787, outside this part).
-- src:15600 | Offence
-- src:15601 | (4) Every person who contravenes subsection (1) or (2) is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref s 732.11(4) (src:15600-15601)
GIVEN `the person contravenes subsection 732.11(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person contravenes subsection 732.11(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 732.11(4) the person is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction` MEANS
    IF `the person contravenes subsection 732.11(1)` OR `the person contravenes subsection 732.11(2)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Every person who contravenes subsection (1) or (2) is guilty of an offence"

@ref s 732.11(4) (src:15600-15601)
`s 732.11(4) the class of offence` MEANS `an offence punishable on summary conviction`

@ref s 732.11(4) (src:15600-15601)
`s 732.11(4) the punishment on summary conviction` MEANS Punishment OF `on summary conviction`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`

§ `Section 732.2 -- Coming into force, duration and change of a probation order`

-- (1): when the order comes into force. (b) and (c) displace (a) in the cases they describe; where both (b) and (c) describe the case the text does not say which governs.
-- src:15602 | Coming into force of order
-- src:15603 | 732.2 (1) A probation order comes into force
-- src:15604 | (a) on the date on which the order is made;
-- src:15605 | (b) where the offender is sentenced to imprisonment under paragraph 731(1)(b) or was previously sentenced to imprisonment for another offence, as soon as the offender is released from prison or, if released from prison on conditional release, at the expiration of the sentence of imprisonment; or
-- src:15606 | (c) where the offender is under a conditional sentence order, at the expiration of the conditional sentence order.
@ref s 732.2(1) (src:15602-15606)
DECLARE `s 732.2(1) coming into force` IS ONE OF
    `s 732.2(1)(a) on the date on which the order is made`
    `s 732.2(1)(b) as soon as the offender is released from prison or, if released from prison on conditional release, at the expiration of the sentence of imprisonment`
    `s 732.2(1)(c) at the expiration of the conditional sentence order`

@ref s 732.2(1) (src:15602-15606)
GIVEN `the offender is sentenced to imprisonment under paragraph 731(1)(b) or was previously sentenced to imprisonment for another offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the offender is under a conditional sentence order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 732.2(1) coming into force`
`s 732.2(1) when the probation order comes into force` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the offender is sentenced to imprisonment under paragraph 731(1)(b) or was previously sentenced to imprisonment for another offence` AND `the offender is under a conditional sentence order` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text does not say which of paragraphs (b) and (c) governs when both describe the offender
        IF `the offender is under a conditional sentence order` THEN JUST `s 732.2(1)(c) at the expiration of the conditional sentence order`
        IF `the offender is sentenced to imprisonment under paragraph 731(1)(b) or was previously sentenced to imprisonment for another offence` THEN JUST `s 732.2(1)(b) as soon as the offender is released from prison or, if released from prison on conditional release, at the expiration of the sentence of imprisonment`
        OTHERWISE JUST `s 732.2(1)(a) on the date on which the order is made`

@ref s 732.2(1) (src:15602-15606)
GIVEN `the date on which the order is made` IS A DATE
      `the offender is sentenced to imprisonment under paragraph 731(1)(b) or was previously sentenced to imprisonment for another offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the offender is released from prison` IS A DATE
      `the offender is released from prison on conditional release` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date of the expiration of the sentence of imprisonment` IS A DATE
      `the offender is under a conditional sentence order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date of the expiration of the conditional sentence order` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 732.2(1) the date on which the probation order comes into force` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the offender is sentenced to imprisonment under paragraph 731(1)(b) or was previously sentenced to imprisonment for another offence` AND `the offender is under a conditional sentence order` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text does not say which of paragraphs (b) and (c) governs when both describe the offender
        IF `the offender is under a conditional sentence order` THEN JUST `the date of the expiration of the conditional sentence order`
        IF `the offender is sentenced to imprisonment under paragraph 731(1)(b) or was previously sentenced to imprisonment for another offence` AND `the offender is released from prison on conditional release` THEN JUST `the date of the expiration of the sentence of imprisonment`
        IF `the offender is sentenced to imprisonment under paragraph 731(1)(b) or was previously sentenced to imprisonment for another offence` THEN JUST `the date the offender is released from prison`
        OTHERWISE JUST `the date on which the order is made`

-- (2)(a): "Subject to subsection (5)": the function does not compute (5), which is a power of the court.
-- src:15607 | Duration of order and limit on term of order
-- src:15608 | (2) Subject to subsection (5),
-- src:15609 | (a) where an offender who is bound by a probation order is convicted of an offence, including an offence under section 733.1, or is imprisoned under paragraph 731(1)(b) in default of payment of a fine, the order continues in force except in so far as the sentence renders it impossible for the offender for the time being to comply with the order; and
-- src:15610 | (b) no probation order shall continue in force for more than three years after the date on which the order came into force.
@ref s 732.2(2) (src:15607-15610)
GIVEN `the offender who is bound by a probation order is convicted of an offence, including an offence under section 733.1, or is imprisoned under paragraph 731(1)(b) in default of payment of a fine` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the sentence renders it impossible for the offender for the time being to comply with the order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 732.2(2)(a) this paragraph keeps the order in force` MEANS   -- gate: where (an offender bound by a probation order is convicted, or imprisoned in default of payment of a fine)
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the offender who is bound by a probation order is convicted of an offence, including an offence under section 733.1, or is imprisoned under paragraph 731(1)(b) in default of payment of a fine` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where an offender who is bound by a probation order is convicted of an offence, including an offence under section 733.1, or is imprisoned under paragraph 731(1)(b) in default of payment of a fine, the order continues in force"
        IF `the sentence renders it impossible for the offender for the time being to comply with the order` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "except in so far as the sentence renders it impossible for the offender for the time being to comply with the order"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

@ref s 732.2(2)(b) (src:15607-15610)
GIVEN `the date on which the order came into force` IS A DATE
      `the date in question` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 732.2(2)(b) the date is within the three years after the order came into force` MEANS
    IF `the date in question` AT MOST (`add years` `the date on which the order came into force` 3)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "no probation order shall continue in force for more than three years after the date on which the order came into force"

-- (3): changes on application. The "at any time" and the "on application" are gates of the kind "on"; the "after hearing" is a gate of the kind "after".
-- src:15611 | Changes to probation order
-- src:15612 | (3) A court that makes a probation order may at any time, on application by the offender, the probation officer or the prosecutor, require the offender to appear before it and, after hearing the offender and one or both of the probation officer and the prosecutor,
-- src:15613 | (a) make any changes to the optional conditions that in the opinion of the court are rendered desirable by a change in the circumstances since those conditions were prescribed,
-- src:15614 | (b) relieve the offender, either absolutely or on such terms or for such period as the court deems desirable, of compliance with any optional condition, or
-- src:15615 | (c) decrease the period for which the probation order is to remain in force,
-- src:15616 | and the court shall thereupon endorse the probation order accordingly and, if it changes the optional conditions, inform the offender of its action and give the offender a copy of the order so endorsed.
@ref s 732.2(3) (src:15611-15616)
GIVEN `the court is a court that makes a probation order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the offender, the probation officer or the prosecutor applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 732.2(3) the court may require the offender to appear before it` MEANS   -- gate: on (application by the offender, the probation officer or the prosecutor)
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the court is a court that makes a probation order` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A court that makes a probation order may"
        IF NOT `the offender, the probation officer or the prosecutor applies` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "on application by the offender, the probation officer or the prosecutor"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

@ref s 732.2(3)(a) (src:15611-15613)
GIVEN `the court is a court that makes a probation order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court has heard the offender and one or both of the probation officer and the prosecutor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the changes are, in the opinion of the court, rendered desirable by a change in the circumstances since the optional conditions were prescribed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 732.2(3)(a) the court may make the changes to the optional conditions` MEANS   -- gate: after (hearing the offender and one or both of the probation officer and the prosecutor); if (the changes are rendered desirable by a change in the circumstances)
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the court is a court that makes a probation order` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A court that makes a probation order may"
        IF NOT `the court has heard the offender and one or both of the probation officer and the prosecutor` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "after hearing the offender and one or both of the probation officer and the prosecutor"
        IF NOT `the changes are, in the opinion of the court, rendered desirable by a change in the circumstances since the optional conditions were prescribed` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "make any changes to the optional conditions that in the opinion of the court are rendered desirable by a change in the circumstances since those conditions were prescribed"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

@ref s 732.2(3)(b) (src:15611-15614)
GIVEN `the court is a court that makes a probation order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court has heard the offender and one or both of the probation officer and the prosecutor` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 732.2(3)(b) the court may relieve the offender of compliance with an optional condition` MEANS   -- gate: after (hearing the offender and one or both of the probation officer and the prosecutor)
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the court is a court that makes a probation order` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A court that makes a probation order may"
        IF NOT `the court has heard the offender and one or both of the probation officer and the prosecutor` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "after hearing the offender and one or both of the probation officer and the prosecutor"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

@ref s 732.2(3)(c) (src:15611-15616)
GIVEN `the court is a court that makes a probation order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court has heard the offender and one or both of the probation officer and the prosecutor` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 732.2(3)(c) the court may decrease the period for which the probation order is to remain in force` MEANS   -- gate: after (hearing the offender and one or both of the probation officer and the prosecutor)
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the court is a court that makes a probation order` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A court that makes a probation order may"
        IF NOT `the court has heard the offender and one or both of the probation officer and the prosecutor` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "after hearing the offender and one or both of the probation officer and the prosecutor"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

@ref s 732.2(3)(c) (src:15615-15616)
GIVEN `the court has made a change under subsection 732.2(3)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 732.2(3) the court must endorse the probation order accordingly` MEANS
    IF `the court has made a change under subsection 732.2(3)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the court shall thereupon endorse the probation order accordingly"

@ref s 732.2(3)(c) (src:15615-15616)
GIVEN `the court has made a change under subsection 732.2(3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the change is to the optional conditions` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 732.2(3) the court must inform the offender and give the offender a copy of the order so endorsed` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the court has made a change under subsection 732.2(3)` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the court shall thereupon endorse the probation order accordingly and, if it changes the optional conditions, inform the offender of its action"
        IF `the change is to the optional conditions` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if it changes the optional conditions, inform the offender of its action and give the offender a copy of the order so endorsed"

-- (4): in chambers.
-- src:15617 | Judge may act in chambers
-- src:15618 | (4) All the functions of the court under subsection (3) may be exercised in chambers.
@ref s 732.2(4) (src:15617-15618)
GIVEN `the function is a function of the court under subsection 732.2(3)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 732.2(4) the court may exercise the function in chambers` MEANS   -- gate: none
    IF `the function is a function of the court under subsection 732.2(3)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "All the functions of the court under subsection (3) may be exercised in chambers"

-- (5): where a bound offender is convicted and the conviction is final.
-- src:15619 | Where person convicted of offence
-- src:15620 | (5) Where an offender who is bound by a probation order is convicted of an offence, including an offence under section 733.1, and
-- src:15621 | (a) the time within which an appeal may be taken against that conviction has expired and the offender has not taken an appeal,
-- src:15622 | (b) the offender has taken an appeal against that conviction and the appeal has been dismissed, or
-- src:15623 | (c) the offender has given written notice to the court that convicted the offender that the offender elects not to appeal the conviction or has abandoned the appeal, as the case may be,
-- src:15624 | in addition to any punishment that may be imposed for that offence, the court that made the probation order may, on application by the prosecutor, require the offender to appear before it and, after hearing the prosecutor and the offender,
-- src:15625 | (d) where the probation order was made under paragraph 731(1)(a), revoke the order and impose any sentence that could have been imposed if the passing of sentence had not been suspended, or
-- src:15626 | (e) make such changes to the optional conditions as the court deems desirable, or extend the period for which the order is to remain in force for such period, not exceeding one year, as the court deems desirable,
-- src:15627 | and the court shall thereupon endorse the probation order accordingly and, if it changes the optional conditions or extends the period for which the order is to remain in force, inform the offender of its action and give the offender a copy of the order so endorsed.
-- src:15628 | Compelling appearance of person bound
-- src:15629 | (6) The provisions of Parts XVI and XVIII with respect to compelling the appearance of an accused before a justice apply, with such modifications as the circumstances require, to proceedings under subsections (3) and (5).
@ref s 732.2(5) (src:15619-15629)
GIVEN `the court is the court that made the probation order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the offender who is bound by a probation order is convicted of an offence, including an offence under section 733.1` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the time within which an appeal may be taken against the conviction has expired and the offender has not taken an appeal` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the offender has taken an appeal against the conviction and the appeal has been dismissed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the offender has given written notice to the court that convicted the offender that the offender elects not to appeal the conviction or has abandoned the appeal` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the prosecutor applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 732.2(5) the court may require the offender to appear before it` MEANS   -- gate: where (an offender bound by a probation order is convicted and the conviction is final), on (application by the prosecutor)
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the offender who is bound by a probation order is convicted of an offence, including an offence under section 733.1` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where an offender who is bound by a probation order is convicted of an offence, including an offence under section 733.1"
        IF NOT (`the time within which an appeal may be taken against the conviction has expired and the offender has not taken an appeal` OR `the offender has taken an appeal against the conviction and the appeal has been dismissed` OR `the offender has given written notice to the court that convicted the offender that the offender elects not to appeal the conviction or has abandoned the appeal`) THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the time within which an appeal may be taken against that conviction has expired and the offender has not taken an appeal"
        IF NOT `the court is the court that made the probation order` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the court that made the probation order may"
        IF NOT `the prosecutor applies` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "on application by the prosecutor"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

@ref s 732.2(5)(d) (src:15619-15625)
GIVEN `the court is the court that made the probation order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the probation order was made under paragraph 731(1)(a)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court has heard the prosecutor and the offender` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 732.2(5)(d) the court may revoke the order and impose any sentence that could have been imposed if the passing of sentence had not been suspended` MEANS   -- gate: where (the probation order was made under paragraph 731(1)(a)), after (hearing the prosecutor and the offender)
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the probation order was made under paragraph 731(1)(a)` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where the probation order was made under paragraph 731(1)(a), revoke the order"
        IF NOT `the court has heard the prosecutor and the offender` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "after hearing the prosecutor and the offender"
        IF NOT `the court is the court that made the probation order` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the court that made the probation order may"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

@ref s 732.2(5)(e) (src:15619-15629)
GIVEN `the court is the court that made the probation order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court has heard the prosecutor and the offender` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court extends the period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the extension of the period` IS A `Length of time`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 732.2(5)(e) the court may make changes to the optional conditions or extend the period for which the order is to remain in force` MEANS   -- gate: after (hearing the prosecutor and the offender); limit of the grant (an extension not exceeding one year)
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the court has heard the prosecutor and the offender` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "after hearing the prosecutor and the offender"
        IF NOT `the court is the court that made the probation order` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the court that made the probation order may"
        IF `the court extends the period` AND (`s 716 the first period is at most the second period` `the extension of the period` (`Length of time` OF 1, 0, 0, FALSE)) EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "extend the period for which the order is to remain in force for such period, not exceeding one year, as the court deems desirable"
        IF `the court extends the period` AND (`s 716 the first period is at most the second period` `the extension of the period` (`Length of time` OF 1, 0, 0, FALSE)) EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the extension is a year or less is not settled by the calendar
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

@ref s 732.2(5)(e) (src:15626-15629)
GIVEN `the court has made a change under subsection 732.2(5)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 732.2(5) the court must endorse the probation order accordingly` MEANS
    IF `the court has made a change under subsection 732.2(5)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the court shall thereupon endorse the probation order accordingly"

@ref s 732.2(5)(e) (src:15626-15629)
GIVEN `the court has made a change under subsection 732.2(5)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the change is to the optional conditions or extends the period` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 732.2(5) the court must inform the offender and give the offender a copy of the order so endorsed` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the court has made a change under subsection 732.2(5)` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the court shall thereupon endorse the probation order accordingly and, if it changes the optional conditions or extends the period for which the order is to remain in force, inform the offender of its action"
        IF `the change is to the optional conditions or extends the period` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if it changes the optional conditions or extends the period for which the order is to remain in force, inform the offender of its action and give the offender a copy of the order so endorsed"

-- src:15628 | Compelling appearance of person bound
-- src:15629 | (6) The provisions of Parts XVI and XVIII with respect to compelling the appearance of an accused before a justice apply, with such modifications as the circumstances require, to proceedings under subsections (3) and (5).
@ref s 732.2(6) (src:15628-15629)
GIVEN `the proceeding is a proceeding under subsection 732.2(3) or (5)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 732.2(6) the provisions of Parts XVI and XVIII for compelling the appearance of an accused apply to the proceeding` MEANS
    IF `the proceeding is a proceeding under subsection 732.2(3) or (5)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "apply, with such modifications as the circumstances require, to proceedings under subsections (3) and (5)"

§ `Section 733 -- Transfer of order`

-- (1.1): the consent the transfer needs. "only with (a) ... or (b) ..." closes the gate: a missing consent that applies answers JUST FALSE.
-- src:15632 | Attorney General’s consent
-- src:15633 | (1.1) The transfer may be granted only with
-- src:15634 | (a) the consent of the Attorney General of the province in which the probation order was made, if the two territorial divisions are not in the same province; or
-- src:15635 | (b) the consent of the Attorney General of Canada, if the proceedings that led to the issuance of the probation order were instituted by or on behalf of the Attorney General of Canada.
@ref s 733(1.1) (src:15632-15635)
GIVEN `the two territorial divisions are not in the same province` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Attorney General of the province in which the probation order was made consents` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the proceedings that led to the issuance of the probation order were instituted by or on behalf of the Attorney General of Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Attorney General of Canada consents` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 733(1.1) the consent the transfer needs has been given` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the two territorial divisions are not in the same province` OR `the proceedings that led to the issuance of the probation order were instituted by or on behalf of the Attorney General of Canada`) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): neither paragraph (a) nor paragraph (b) describes the transfer, and the subsection says nothing of it
        IF `the two territorial divisions are not in the same province` AND (NOT `the Attorney General of the province in which the probation order was made consents`) THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the consent of the Attorney General of the province in which the probation order was made, if the two territorial divisions are not in the same province"
        IF `the proceedings that led to the issuance of the probation order were instituted by or on behalf of the Attorney General of Canada` AND (NOT `the Attorney General of Canada consents`) THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the consent of the Attorney General of Canada, if the proceedings that led to the issuance of the probation order were instituted by or on behalf of the Attorney General of Canada"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- (1): the transfer.
-- src:15630 | Transfer of order
-- src:15631 | 733 (1) Where an offender who is bound by a probation order becomes a resident of, or is convicted or discharged under section 730 of an offence including an offence under section 733.1 in, a territorial division other than the territorial division where the order was made, on the application of a probation officer, the court that made the order may, subject to subsection (1.1), transfer the order to a court in that other territorial division that would, having regard to the mode of trial of the offender, have had jurisdiction to make the order in that other territorial division if the offender had been tried and convicted there of the offence in respect of which the order was made, and the order may thereafter be dealt with and enforced by the court to which it is so transferred in all respects as if that court had made the order.
@ref s 733(1) (src:15630-15631)
GIVEN `the court is the court that made the probation order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the offender who is bound by a probation order becomes a resident of, or is convicted or discharged under section 730 in, a territorial division other than the territorial division where the order was made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a probation officer applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the consent the transfer needs has been given` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the court to which the order is transferred would, having regard to the mode of trial of the offender, have had jurisdiction to make the order there if the offender had been tried and convicted there of the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 733(1) the court that made the order may transfer the order` MEANS   -- gate: where (the offender becomes a resident of, or is convicted or discharged in, another territorial division), on (application of a probation officer), only with (the consents of subsection (1.1))
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the offender who is bound by a probation order becomes a resident of, or is convicted or discharged under section 730 in, a territorial division other than the territorial division where the order was made` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where an offender who is bound by a probation order becomes a resident of, or is convicted or discharged under section 730 of an offence including an offence under section 733.1 in, a territorial division other than the territorial division where the order was made"
        IF NOT `a probation officer applies` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "on the application of a probation officer"
        IF `the consent the transfer needs has been given` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The transfer may be granted only with"
        IF NOT `the court is the court that made the probation order` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the court that made the order may"
        IF NOT `the court to which the order is transferred would, having regard to the mode of trial of the offender, have had jurisdiction to make the order there if the offender had been tried and convicted there of the offence` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "to a court in that other territorial division that would, having regard to the mode of trial of the offender, have had jurisdiction to make the order"
        IF `the consent the transfer needs has been given` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether a consent is needed is left open by subsection (1.1)
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:15636 | Where court unable to act
-- src:15637 | (2) Where a court that has made a probation order or to which a probation order has been transferred pursuant to subsection (1) is for any reason unable to act, the powers of that court in relation to the probation order may be exercised by any other court that has equivalent jurisdiction in the same province.
@ref s 733(2) (src:15636-15637)
GIVEN `a court that has made a probation order or to which a probation order has been transferred is for any reason unable to act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the other court has equivalent jurisdiction in the same province` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 733(2) another court may exercise the powers of the court in relation to the probation order` MEANS   -- gate: where (the court is for any reason unable to act)
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `a court that has made a probation order or to which a probation order has been transferred is for any reason unable to act` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a court that has made a probation order or to which a probation order has been transferred pursuant to subsection (1) is for any reason unable to act, the powers of that court in relation to the probation order may be exercised by any other court"
        IF NOT `the other court has equivalent jurisdiction in the same province` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any other court that has equivalent jurisdiction in the same province"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§ `Section 733.1 -- Failure to comply with probation order`

-- src:15638 | Failure to comply with probation order
-- src:15639 | 733.1 (1) An offender who is bound by a probation order and who, without reasonable excuse, fails or refuses to comply with that order is guilty of
@ref s 733.1(1) (src:15638-15639)
GIVEN `the offender is bound by a probation order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the offender fails or refuses to comply with the order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the offender has a reasonable excuse` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 733.1(1) the offender is guilty of failing to comply with the probation order` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the offender is bound by a probation order` AND `the offender fails or refuses to comply with the order`) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "An offender who is bound by a probation order and who, without reasonable excuse, fails or refuses to comply with that order is guilty of"
        IF `the offender has a reasonable excuse` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "without reasonable excuse"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:15638 | Failure to comply with probation order
-- src:15639 | 733.1 (1) An offender who is bound by a probation order and who, without reasonable excuse, fails or refuses to comply with that order is guilty of
-- src:15640 | (a) an indictable offence and is liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than four years; or
-- src:15641 | (b) an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref s 733.1(1) (src:15638-15641)
@ref s 733.1(1)(a) (src:15640)
`s 733.1(1)(a) four years` MEANS `Length of time` OF 4, 0, 0, FALSE

@ref s 733.1(1)(a) (src:15640)
`s 733.1(1)(a) the punishment on indictment` MEANS Punishment OF `by indictment`, (`imprisonment for a term of` `s 733.1(1)(a) four years`), `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`

@ref s 733.1(1)(b) (src:15641)
`s 733.1(1)(b) the punishment on summary conviction` MEANS Punishment OF `on summary conviction`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`

@ref s 733.1(1) (src:15638-15641)
`s 733.1(1) the class of offence` MEANS `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`

-- (2): the place of trial, and the bar on instituting proceedings outside the province.
-- src:15642 | Where accused may be tried and punished
-- src:15643 | (2) An accused who is charged with an offence under subsection (1) may be tried and punished by any court having jurisdiction to try that offence in the place where the offence is alleged to have been committed or in the place where the accused is found, is arrested or is in custody, but where the place where the accused is found, is arrested or is in custody is outside the province in which the offence is alleged to have been committed, no proceedings in respect of that offence shall be instituted in that place without the consent of the Attorney General of that province.
@ref s 733.1(2) (src:15642-15643)
GIVEN `the accused is charged with an offence under subsection 733.1(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court has jurisdiction to try that offence in the place where it is alleged to have been committed or in the place where the accused is found, is arrested or is in custody` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 733.1(2) the accused may be tried and punished by the court` MEANS   -- gate: none (the limits are on whose case and which courts)
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the accused is charged with an offence under subsection 733.1(1)` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "An accused who is charged with an offence under subsection (1)"
        IF `the court has jurisdiction to try that offence in the place where it is alleged to have been committed or in the place where the accused is found, is arrested or is in custody` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "by any court having jurisdiction to try that offence in the place where the offence is alleged to have been committed or in the place where the accused is found, is arrested or is in custody"

@ref s 733.1(2) (src:15642-15643)
GIVEN `the place where the accused is found, is arrested or is in custody is outside the province in which the offence is alleged to have been committed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Attorney General of that province consents` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 733.1(2) the bar on instituting proceedings in that place applies` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the place where the accused is found, is arrested or is in custody is outside the province in which the offence is alleged to have been committed` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "but where the place where the accused is found, is arrested or is in custody is outside the province in which the offence is alleged to have been committed, no proceedings in respect of that offence shall be instituted in that place without the consent of the Attorney General of that province"
        IF `the Attorney General of that province consents` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "without the consent of the Attorney General of that province"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE
